  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c **** 
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  /**
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @brief Processing function for Q31 LMS filter.
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  *S points to an instance of the Q15 LMS filter structure.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  *pSrc points to the block of input data.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  *pRef points to the block of reference data.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pOut points to the block of output data.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pErr points to the block of error data.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  blockSize number of samples to process.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * @return     none.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * \par Scaling and Overflow Behavior:
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * The function is implemented using an internal 64-bit accumulator.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * The accumulator has a 2.62 format and maintains full precision of the intermediate
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * multiplication results but provides only a single guard bit.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator result overflows it wraps around rather than clips.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * log2(numTaps) bits.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * The reference signal should not be scaled down.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * After all multiply-accumulates are performed, the 2.62 accumulator is shifted
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * and saturated to 1.31 format to yield the final result.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * The output signal and error signal are in 1.31 format.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  *
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * \par
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  * 	In this filter, filter coefficients are updated for each sample and the updation of filter coff
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c ****  */
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_q31.c **** 
